# ReplyCators - Code Ownership
#
# Requires branch protection to be effective.
# Enable "Require review from Code Owners" in GitHub Settings > Branches > main.
#
# Format: <file-pattern>  <@owner>
# Replace @owner with the actual GitHub username(s) of the project maintainer(s).
# Example: AGENTS.md  @jnytko
#
# Documentation: https://docs.github.com/en/repositories/managing-your-repositorys-settings-and-features/customizing-your-repository/about-code-owners

# ── Repository governance files ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# Changes to the authoritative briefing or changelog require owner review.
AGENTS.md                          @owner
CHANGELOG.md                       @owner
PLUGIN-SDK.md                      @owner

# ── Extension manifest ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Any permission, host_permission, or web_accessible_resources change is security-sensitive.
manifest.json                      @owner
dist/manifest.json                 @owner

# ── CI/CD pipeline ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Changes to workflows affect all contributors and CI behaviour.
.github/                           @owner

# ── Application orchestrator ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# High regression risk - changes here can silently break unrelated plugins.
dashboard.js                       @owner
dist/dashboard.js                  @owner

# ── Background service worker ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
background.js                      @owner
dist/background.js                 @owner

# ── Security policy ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
SECURITY.md                        @owner
tools/bob-helper-server.js         @owner
